# Data and heavy outputs
implementations/**/data/
implementations/**/outputs/
*.ckpt
*.pt

# Paper PDFs: not versioned.
# 1) Weight: the git history would grow by hundreds of MB, permanently.
# 2) Copyright: this repo is public (a portfolio); redistributing published
#    PDFs (Annals of Statistics, JMLR, NeurIPS, IEEE...) is not appropriate.
# The inventory with the download links lives in papers/INDEX.md, which IS
# versioned — it is what adds value and it is shareable.
papers/*.pdf
!papers/INDEX.md

# Personal notes: not published. They are in Spanish, unlike everything that is
# committed, precisely because they are not for anyone else.
GUIA-LECTURA.md
REPASO.md

# Obsidian. The repo is also usable as a vault — the reviews and derivations are
# markdown and the PDFs are right there — and opening it creates this folder:
# workspace layout, plugin state and per-machine preferences. None of it is about
# the papers. Note that Obsidian's own [[wikilinks]] and ![[embeds]] render as
# literal text on GitHub, so anything committed keeps standard markdown links;
# turn off "Use [[Wikilinks]]" in Settings → Files & Links.
.obsidian/

# Claude Code local permissions: machine-specific and personal. They accumulate
# allowed commands from whatever is being worked on, including other projects,
# so they do not belong in a repo meant to be read by others. The shared part
# of the configuration — CLAUDE.md and .claude/skills/ — IS versioned.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Internship search: CV, motivation letters, application calendar and
# preparation plan. It is personal material and also strategic — publishing
# which firms are being applied to, and when, works against the applicant. It
# lives outside the repo. The quant READING track does stay: it is in
# ROADMAP.md, section "Quant papers for the /paper workflow".
quant/

# Work in progress, not published until it is understood in depth.
# Lasso: the reproduction of Table 3 (Sec. 7) runs and the ordering of methods
# comes out, but the error levels do not match under any sigma and the
# diagnosis depends on a simulation setup that is not yet commanded. It stays
# local until then; what is published is the solver, the prostate data and the
# cross-check against sklearn, which are closed.
implementations/1996-tibshirani-lasso/simulation.py
implementations/1996-tibshirani-lasso/competitors.py
implementations/1996-tibshirani-lasso/NOTAS-LOCALES.md
